From 45463daf349e91e4441837ecc4fb55caf8f4fc17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:25:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Bindings: layouts of the arrays and padding of the material
 managers

The C bindings get an enumeration of the arrays (mgis_bv_MaterialArray)
and functions setting and getting the layout of one array and the
padding, on the initializer and on the managers. The functions getting
the single layout of a manager report an error if the layouts of its
arrays differ. The Fortran bindings wrap the same functions, and their
accessors returning multidimensional arrays check the layout and the
padding of the array they return.
---
 .../MGIS/Behaviour/MaterialDataManager.h      |  65 +++-
 .../MGIS/Behaviour/MaterialStateManager.h     |  61 +++-
 bindings/c/src/MaterialDataManager.cxx        | 135 +++++++-
 bindings/c/src/MaterialStateManager.cxx       |  66 +++-
 bindings/fortran/src/mgis_behaviour.f90       | 294 +++++++++++++++++-
 5 files changed, 595 insertions(+), 26 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bindings/c/include/MGIS/Behaviour/MaterialDataManager.h b/bindings/c/include/MGIS/Behaviour/MaterialDataManager.h
